  {
   "slug": "theres-music-in-dem-darn-hills",
   "title": "There’s Music In Dem Darn Hills",
   "by": "",
   "year": "2022",
   "genre": "Ambient",
   "wash": "#8a3c12",
   "sc": "https://soundcloud.com/chemtrails/sets/theres-music-in-dem-darn-hills",
   "total": "1:11:38",
   "desc": "Historic field recordings collide with contemporary production—past and present stitched together with a cold, steady hand. This isn’t nostalgia. It’s excavation: degraded voices, distant rooms, damaged tape, and fragments that were never meant to outlive the moment.\n\nEach track lands like evidence—part document, part séance—where modern drums act as a heartbeat beneath something older that won’t stay quiet. You can hear the air in the room, the warble of the reel, the ghost of a sentence cut off mid-thought. Memory becomes texture. Silence becomes threat. The closer you listen, the more you listen, the recording are listening back.\n\nHeadphones recommended.  The past isn’t resonating... It’s waking up.",
